 "briefing": "# Infosys Briefing: 16 October to 15 November 2026\n\n## Bottom Line\n\nNo Infosys developments from the 30-day window (16 October to 15 November 2026) could be verified. Every search returned an error, so this briefing contains no verified news, launches, hires, or deals. The gap reflects a failed search tool, not a confirmed absence of activity. Before 17 November, the official newsroom, investor relations pages, and exchange filings should be checked directly (see the list below).\n\n## Research Status\n\nAll search attempts returned \"No valid search results found. Please try different search queries or use a different search API.\" No article, press release, filing, or page was retrieved or opened, so no items meet the verification standard (publication date and source URL). Nothing has been inferred or added to fill the gap.\n\n## News\n\nNot verified. No corporate news, earnings or guidance updates, dividend or buyback announcements, board decisions, regulatory developments, or analyst rating changes could be confirmed for the window. Check the [Infosys newsroom](https://www.infosys.com/newsroom) and [Infosys investor relations](https://investors.infosys.com) first.\n\n## Product and Service Launches\n\nNot verified. No platform, product, or service launches could be confirmed. Named offerings such as Topaz and Cobalt were searched without success, so announcements under those names should be checked directly on the newsroom.\n\n## Executive and Other Hires\n\nNot verified. No executive appointments, departures, board changes, country or regional head roles, or large hiring or workforce announcements could be confirmed. Exchange filings for key managerial personnel changes are the most reliable place to check, through [NSE](https://www.nseindia.com) and [BSE](https://www.bseindia.com).\n\n## Deals\n\nNot verified. No partnerships, acquisitions, stake purchases, client contract wins, joint ventures, or investments could be confirmed. Foreign-listed reporting is filed with the [SEC](https://www.sec.gov/edgar), so Form 6-K filings are worth checking alongside the exchange announcements.\n\n## Pages to Check Before the Meeting\n\n- Infosys newsroom and press releases, for news, launches, and partnerships\n- Infosys investor relations, for results, dividends, buybacks, and filings\n- NSE and BSE corporate announcements for Infosys (BSE scrip code 500209), filtered to 16 October to 15 November 2026\n- SEC EDGAR Form 6-K filings for Infosys Limited\n- Economic Times, Mint, Business Standard, Moneycontrol, Reuters, and Bloomberg, filtered to the same window\n\n## Open Questions for Infosys\n\n1. Which material announcements, including exchange disclosures, did Infosys make between 16 October and 15 November 2026, and where are they published?\n2. Have there been any changes to the senior leadership team or board since mid-October, and are any further changes expected before year-end?\n3. Which partnerships, client wins, or acquisitions from the past month should we treat as strategically significant for our engagement?\n\n## Sources\n\n[1] Infosys Newsroom: https://www.infosys.com/newsroom\n[2] Infosys Investor Relations: https://investors.infosys.com\n[3] National Stock Exchange of India: https://www.nseindia.com\n[4] BSE Limited: https://www.bseindia.com\n[5] SEC EDGAR: https://www.sec.gov/edgar",
